course: dictionary
lesson: 7702
title: Short forms: PS
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: PS is an abbreviation, a short form of a longer word. It stands for «postscript», an extra note added at the end of a letter or email, after the signature. «PS Give the dog a hug from me.» The writer has already signed their name, then adds one more thought below it.
explain: You may also see PS in other places. In UK schools it can be short for «primary school», or it can be part of a name like «PS4», a games console. When you meet PS, read the words around it to see which meaning fits.
explain: If you want to add a second extra note, write PPS, as in «PPS I love you». Each extra note goes below the one before it, so PS comes first and PPS comes after.
fact: PS is an abbreviation, a short form of a longer word.
fact: PS is short for postscript: an extra note at the end of a letter or email.
fact: PS is written after your signature, below your name.
fact: A second extra note is PPS.
fact: Words with silent first letters are found under their real spelling: psychology under ps, knee under kn.
exercise: «PS Give the dog a hug from me.» What does PS mean at the bottom of this letter? | A signature with your name | *A postscript, an extra note added at the end | A part number for a games console | A primary school in the town
exercise: Ella's brother has a box with «PS4» on it. What does PS mean here? | Post office | Primary school | Postscript | *Part of a part number for a games console
exercise: Where do you write PS in a letter? | Only on the envelope | In the middle of the second paragraph | *At the bottom, after your name | At the very top, before Dear
test: In a letter, where should PS go? | At the very start, before Dear | *At the bottom, after your name | Only in the title | In the middle of the second line
test: What is a second extra note called? | *PPS | PSS | SPP | PP
exam: Which word is PS short for in a letter? | Primary school | Postal service | Pencil sharpener | *Postscript
